<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_font_bold ltx_title_subsection">A.2  Additional Heatmaps for top-K sensitivity</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.2 Additional Heatmaps for top-K sensitivity ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ LExI: Layer-Adaptive Active Experts for Efficient MoE Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> illustrates the topk sensitivity heatmaps for MiniCPM-MoE and DeepSeekV2 Lite Chat model based on Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Stage 1: Per Layer MoE Top-K Perturbation Profiling: ‣ 4 LExI ‣ LExI: Layer-Adaptive Active Experts for Efficient MoE Model Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F9.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.02753v1/MiniCPM_heatmap.png" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/57;" width="476" height="57" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F9.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.02753v1/DeepSeekV2_heatmap.png" id="A1.F9.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/133;" width="476" height="133" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A1.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Top-<math id="A1.F9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> sensitivity analysis across MiniCPM-MoE-8x2B and DeepSeekV2-Lite. The plots depict the layer-wise output deviation with respect to changing the top-<math id="A1.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. The initial layers in MiniCPM model are less sensitive to topk perturbation than deeper layers, while DeepSeekV2 exhibits a bell curve pattern where initial and last layers are more sensitive.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
